@clawsweeper re-review

Addressed the successful all-cache-hit rebuild retention finding in b1d2cdcd5cd59d3e272067381275823d4b47aca4. The new SQLite regression failed with three cache rows at a cap of one, then passed after pruning the canonical cache only after successful publication. Failed-rebuild preservation remains covered.

Also corrected the three CI chunk-publication tests to verify both intended contracts: published index tables roll back on failure, while completed embeddings remain cached and are reused without additional provider calls. All 71 focused tests, the complete changed-file gate, and final staged P0–P2 autoreview passed. The PR description now includes these results and existing-database/legacy-schema compatibility boundaries.
